  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe makes one 18cm cake that serves 8 people and takes about 1 hour 35 minutes in total. The result is a tall, wobbling, cotton-soft cake unlike any Western cheesecake."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The key to this cake is a stiff"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "meringue"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "folded gently into the cream cheese mixture. Overmixing deflates it and produces a dense result. Fold in three additions, using a large metal spoon or spatula, until just combined. Do not rush this step."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "cream-cheese",
              "amount": 250,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "at room temperature",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "unsalted-butter",
              "amount": 60,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "cut into cubes",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "whole-milk",
              "amount": 100,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "eggs",
              "amount": 6,
              "unit": null,
              "prepNote": "separated, at room temperature",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "caster-sugar",
              "amount": 140,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "divided",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "cornflour",
              "amount": 30,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "sifted",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "lemon-juice",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oven to 150°C fan. Grease the 18cm round tin and line the base and sides with baking paper, making sure the paper comes 5cm above the rim."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Put the cream cheese, butter and milk in a heatproof bowl over a saucepan of barely simmering water. Stir until smooth and combined. Remove from the heat and leave to cool for 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Beat the egg yolks with 40g of the caster sugar until pale. Stir in the lemon juice. Add this to the cooled cream cheese mixture along with the cornflour. Mix until smooth."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Whisk the egg whites with the electric hand whisk until foamy. Add the remaining 100g of sugar gradually, whisking until you have a stiff, glossy meringue. This is your"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "meringue"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fold the meringue into the cream cheese base in three additions. Use a large spoon and a gentle cutting motion. Stop as soon as no white streaks remain."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour the batter into the prepared tin. Place the tin inside a deep roasting tin. Pour boiling water into the roasting tin to a depth of 2cm. This is the"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "bain-marie"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bake for 25 minutes at 150°C, then reduce the oven to 120°C fan and bake for a further 40 minutes. The cake should be set with a slight wobble in the centre."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Turn the oven off. Open the door slightly and leave the cake inside for 15 minutes. This gradual cooling prevents cracking. Remove and cool completely in the tin before turning out. This is the"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "cotton cheesecake"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "at its best."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Cake cracked on top",
              "cause": "The oven temperature was too high or the cake cooled too quickly.",
              "fix": "Always reduce the temperature partway through and cool in the oven with the door ajar. Do not open the oven during baking."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Cake sank after coming out of the oven",
              "cause": "The meringue was not stiff enough or was overmixed when folded in.",
              "fix": "Whisk egg whites to firm peaks before folding. Use gentle strokes and stop folding as soon as streaks are gone."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Texture is dense and rubbery rather than light",
              "cause": "The egg whites were beaten too far or the batter was overmixed.",
              "fix": "Stop whisking when the whites hold stiff but still glossy peaks. Fold gently and do not overwork the batter once the whites are in."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This style of cheesecake became popular in Japan in the 1990s. It was developed to appeal to Japanese tastes, which favour lighter, less sweet desserts. It takes cues from both Western cheesecake and the Japanese tradition of light sponge cakes. You find it in bakeries and cafes across Japan. It is now made at home all over the world."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}